{"id":"ten-years-to-the-day","title":"Ten years to the day","question":"The Board must also vote on a contract that lasts more than ten years. How many contracts are written for exactly ten?","finding":"201 contracts carry a term of exactly ten years; 17 run up to a month longer, and 82 between ten years and eleven in all. 152 of the 201 are also under $10 million ($474.9 million in all), so neither line reaches them; 9 of those are within 10% of the dollar line as well. They sit mostly with Public Health (54); Public Utilities Commission (23); Homelessness Services (13); Airport Commission (9).","how":"Term length is the recorded end date minus the recorded start date in the Supplier Contracts table. “Exactly ten years” means 3,650 to 3,653 days, which allows for leap days and for terms written to end the day before the anniversary. Construction contracts are left out. Rows are the ten-year contracts under $10 million, largest first.","limits":"On ten-year terms: the rule, as the ballot summary states it, reaches contracts that last more than ten years. Ten years is also a natural round term for software, leases and long service agreements, and many of the largest ten-year contracts are over $10 million and went to the Board anyway. The end date shown is today’s, so a contract that began shorter and was extended up to the ten-year limit looks the same as one written for ten years at the start; telling them apart needs the original agreement. A cluster at a round number is a question about how terms are set, not a finding about any one contract.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"payee","t":"With","type":"org"},{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"contract","t":"Contract","type":"text"},{"k":"number","t":"Contract number","type":"text"},{"k":"start","t":"Term starts","type":"date"},{"k":"end","t":"Term ends","type":"date"},{"k":"agreed","t":"Agreed amount","type":"usd"},{"k":"underLine","t":"Under the $10 million line by","type":"usd"},{"k":"paid"